    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22294v1</id>
    <title>Multi-Target Few-Shot Prompting with Diffusion Language Models</title>
    <updated>2026-10-15T17:44:46Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22294v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.22294v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Few-shot prompting is useful when instructions and rewards are hard to specify. One such application is editing by example, where a demonstrated formatting change or API migration may need to be applied across multiple sites. However, such edits often depend on both left and right context, making generation with causal autoregressive models awkward. We therefore introduce multi-target few-shot prompting with diffusion language models, where examples guide the infilling of multiple masked regions within a shared canvas. To address the known challenge of reliably following demonstrations in few-shot prompting, we further leverage selective masking of the canvas to derive a likelihood-ratio reward that favors example-supported infills. Across few-shot prompting benchmarks and software refactoring case studies, we find that demonstrations improve infilling accuracy, with example guidance yielding further gains in several settings.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-10-15T17:44:46Z</published>
